You could just have a miniature version of the normal nethack screen in
a corner, with maybe red lights for monsters. That way you could see that
a monster was behind you, and turn to see what it was.

>Another factor is Time.  Will it seem strange for the player to have
>realtime direction changing, but non-realtime movement (ie. you take a
>step and all the monsters take a step, then everything is still while
>you look around).

Might and Magic 3-5 (and probably the rest) did this; it didn't seem
strange at all. At least, no stranger than having monsters move when
you do, then stand still while you hunt through your pack for that
wand of magic missle :)

